The '''X-34 landspeeder''' was a model of civilian [[landspeeder]] manufactured by [[SoroSuub Corporation]] and available during the [[Galactic Civil War]] between the [[Galactic Empire]] and the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].

==Characteristics==
[[FIle:MarkIIMediumBlaster-SWL36.jpg|thumb|left|200px|An X-34 landspeeder equipped with a Mark II medium blaster]]
The X-34 was a civilian [[landspeeder]] of mundane design produced by [[SoroSuub Corporation]].<ref name="USW" /> Built with a powerful [[repulsorlift]] engine augmented with three air-cooled thrust turbines, the X-34 hovered up to a [[meter]] off the ground during operation.<ref name="DB" /> The vehicles were capable of crossing rough terrain, and were well-suited for harsh [[desert]] climates. Owners could choose from either an open-air or sealed [[cockpit]], although the [[speeder]]s lacked any form of combat capability in the form of weapon mounts or [[armor]].<ref name="USW" /> The X-34 was fast, if fairly nondescript in appearance, and measured 3.4 meters in length.<ref name="DB" /> X-34 landspeeders utilized by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] were retrofitted with [[blaster cannon]]s,<ref name="Battlefront II" /> such as the [[Mark II EWHB-10|Mark II Medium Blaster]].<ref name="SWL36">{{Legion|set=X-34 Landspeeder Unit Expansion|cardname=Mark II Medium Blaster}}</ref>

==History==
[[File:X34-landspeeder.jpg|thumb|right|270px|Luke Skywalker pilots his X-34 landspeeder through the Jundland Wastes]]
X-34 landspeeders were utilized as civilian [[transport]]s perfect for traveling smoothly over even the roughest terrain. For this reason, they found use in harsh [[desert]] climates,<ref name="USW" /> and were in operation on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="ANH" /> The [[farm]]boy [[Luke Skywalker]] owned an old and battered X-34<ref name="DB" /> which he made extensive use of<ref name="USW" /> to travel through the planet's deserts, leaving the craft sand-pocked and sun-faded, and missing its portside turbine cowling.<ref name="CVNE" /> Skywalker kept the landspeeder in good working order with tinkering and careful maintenance, which proved essential in the desert environment.<ref name="DB" /> He sold the landspeeder in [[Mos Eisley]] for two thousand [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]]<ref name="Everything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> after the [[death]]s of his aunt and uncle, [[Beru Whitesun Lars|Beru]] and [[Owen Lars]], and used the [[Currency|money]] to help pay for transport to the planet [[Alderaan]]. Around this [[time]], following the release of the [[XP-38 sport speeder|XP-38]], demand for X-34s had dropped in favor of the newer model.<ref name="ANH" /> During the [[Galactic Civil War]], the Alliance to Restore the Republic utilized X-34 landspeeders retrofitted with blaster cannons.<ref name="Battlefront II" />

==Behind the scenes==
The X-34 landspeeder first appeared in the film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="ANH" /> For the [[1977]] film, a life-sized prop of the vehicle was used at [[Tunisia]].<ref name="ANH BTS">{{SW|url=a-new-hope-behind-the-scenes|text=''Star Wars: A New Hope'' Behind the Scenes Gallery}}</ref>

